    Tests: serve/test_chat_sidebar.js case 87 runs one stream three ways - no scroll, the page's own follow, and
    the reader scrolling away from the end - and asserts the fold happens in the first two and not the third.
    Controls: marking nothing fails the reader run; dropping the near-end guard fails the follow run.
    Unverified in a browser: nothing marks a block from a real wheel/touch scroll yet, since the stub fires no
    scroll event when script sets scrollTop - the near-end comparison is reasoned, not measured.

`tool-fold-on-next-output`  A finished tool call should stay open until the next output starts, not fold the instant its result lands. [ui] DONE 2026-11-19
    DONE: with "Show thinking" on live, a settled call keeps its block open until the model moves on - a later call,
