        answered attempt, measured on a 290k-token chat: the round's own tail re-read (876-2,366 tokens) plus
        one pass, 1-2 s; five in a row is ~5-10 s against a turn that already runs 60-200 s here.  Controls
        pin the value: set it back to two and both cap tests fail.
        Test: serve/test_mcp.py UnknownCall.test_a_real_round_between_two_slips_does_not_use_the_cap_up
