    sends the baseline back in ONE request ({server, disabled} where a switch moved, plus {server, tools:[...]}
    per live server) rather than replaying inverse clicks.  Both views redraw together: the card by loadMcp (which
    renderMcp is part of), the open panel by redrawMcpViews.
    A bug the human caught by looking: "it always says Apply 1 change, no matter how many I click" - the count was
    mcpPending().length, which is SERVERS, not changes.  The label is gone with Apply; what remains says
    "Undo the N server(s) you changed here", which is what the number actually means.
    Tests: harness case 91 - Undo greyed on open, a switch posts at once, the card moves unprompted, the open
    panel is rebuilt by the page (the test never reopens it, so a page that failed to rebuild now fails), the
    server-count sentence, Undo sends the whole baseline in one request, and the window closes after use.
    Controls: Undo never greyed / the baseline path dropped / no snapshot on open / the open panel not rebuilt -
