`server-before-model`  Start the web server before the model loads, so the page can open while loading. [py] DONE 2026-11-21 (restart needed; not yet seen in a browser)
    Measured and documented in LESSONS.md ("`/health`'s loaded does not mean the model is loaded"): the port
    does not listen until the model is up - httpd = serve(svc, ...) is serve/server.py:6633, AFTER "loading the
    model (the first start takes a minute or two) ..." at server.py:6448 and after the StrataEngine(...)
    constructor. So a page has exactly one signal - "my fetch of /health stopped failing" - and cannot tell
    "still loading" from "not started". That is why the start-up sound is a server-side console bell.
    Fix: bind and serve first, hold generation until the engine is ready. What must not regress:
      - /health and /metrics must answer something sensible while loading, and Service.loaded() must not lie -
        it is not hasattr(engine, "alive") or engine.alive() (server.py:2941-2943) and alive() is just
        proc.poll() is None (server.py:872-875). A page that loads and sees loaded:false needs a "still
        loading" state, which is the other half of this item (the front end has no such state today).
      - the start-waiters path: a restart never hangs a waiter, it ends with a clean 503
        (serve/test_restart_waiters.py, #1012). Same guard must cover "engine not up yet".
      - --open / open_browser opens the page when the MODEL is ready (setup.py:4410 appends --open unless
        open_browser is false); with the server up early, decide whether it opens earlier now.
    Also: the engine is constructed on the main thread today, so loading has to move to a thread or the
    server must be started before it. That is the real work, and it is where the risk is.
    DECIDED 2026-11-21 by the owner, asked because AGENTS.md says new behaviour is opt-in: this one is NOT
    behind a key - "Default, no configuration here. It just works this way now." And for a request that arrives
    while the model is still loading: the FRONT END holds it and sends it when the server is up; the server's
    queue is not redesigned around it.  What the tree already has for this, read 2026-11-21: StrataEngine's
    constructor returns at once with lazy=True (serve/server.py:694), Service.ensure_loaded() starts it under
    the FIFO (:3117), and prepare() already raises EngineStarting -> a 503 "the engine is starting (a minute or
    two)" (:3739, :5595) - so "bind first, load in a thread" is mostly moving the call to the constructor.
    Three things must move with it, or they stop working at all: warn_tight_ram and desktop_vram_note read
    engine.info, which is empty until the engine reports INFO; the start_beep bell belongs to the model being
    ready, not the port; and a config that cannot start the engine now leaves a page open that has to say why.
    SHIPPED 2026-11-21, both halves, no flag (the owner's call).  serve/server.py: the engine and the vision
    encoder are built lazy at every start now, and start_model_load() (next to serve()) brings them up on a
    thread once the port is listening.  It holds the FIFO for the load - the same lock Service.run takes before
    ensure_loaded() - so a request that arrives mid-load waits its turn and is served: measured 200 with one
    restart, not a 503.  What had to move with it, exactly as the notes above warned: warn_tight_ram and
    desktop_vram_note are now post_load_notes(), called once the engine has reported INFO (left where they
    were they would read an empty engine.info and simply stop firing); the start_beep bell moved off the URL
    banner onto a new "model ready: ..., N s" line; --open still opens once the MODEL is ready, because #560
    #516 wants the card note on the console before a browser is started at that card.  /health gained
    `loading`, `load_seconds` and `load_error`, and the banner carries ", model loading" so the "ready: http"
    line LESSONS.md greps for still marks a process boundary.  A model that will not start leaves the server up
    with the reason in it instead of the process dying before a port exists.
    The page (serve/web/app.js): loadHealth() keeps asking every 2 s while loading; healthPill() paints
    "Loading the model" (blue - producing nothing is what that colour already means) or "The model did not
    start" (amber); renderPill() asks it first, so the 1 s metrics poll cannot paint Idle over it; and the
    empty-state line carries the failure's reason rather than claiming a model that is not running.
    Tests: serve/test_web_first_start.py (5, new module) - the three states on /health; a request that arrives
    mid-load is served and does not start a second load; a failed load leaves the server up, reports, and the
    next request loads it and clears the report; the load holds the FIFO; and the wiring itself, with
